@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import {
  delegation, brief text, reply budget,
}
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import {
    task, task id, brief, result, transcript, launch spec, attach command,
  session export, child driver, child session, starter tools,
  prerequisites check,
}
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
  project root, load error, general agent, fallback agent,   agent definition,         agent file, starter entries, timeout, thinking level, model, medium tier,   agents map, tool list, working directory,
}
@design/kernel.sigil from Kernel import {
  driver registry, parent adapter, supported child host, entry point, child host,
}
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import {
    task record, task status, parent session id, start-up sweep,
}

component Cli {
  goal {
    Give a person at a terminal the same delegation as a parent adapter, plus a
    way
    to open and export what a child did after the parent session is gone.
  }

  logic {
    Every command starts through the delegation service, so that the
    start-up sweep runs first. On subzero run, make a delegation from the agent
    name given with the agent option, which may be left out, and the brief text
    in
    the arguments, with no parent session id, wait
    for
    it
    and print the result. When no agent name is given or the agent name is
    general, the general agent runs. When the agent name is a name other than
    general that the
    agents map does not hold runs the fallback agent and the printed result
    says
    that the
    named
    agent is not configured. When the
    agent file fails to load, print the load error to stderr and exit non-zero
    the same way. On subzero init, take a model from the arguments and, from
    named
    options, the option host, which names the child host, a timeout that
    defaults
    to 1200 seconds and a
    thinking level
    that defaults to medium, where the option host may be left out when
    exactly one
    supported child host is registered, and ask the driver registry for the
    prerequisites check of the child driver of that child host and run it, when
    it
    offers one, before anything is written: when it returns a message, print
    the
    message to stderr and exit non-zero with every file unchanged. Then ask the
    driver registry for the starter tools of that child driver, and ask
    AgentConfig to add the
    starter entries to the agent file under the project root that the
    delegation
    service resolved: the medium tier with that child host, that model and that
    thinking level, a general agent with the tool list for a general agent and
    a
    fallback agent with the tool list that only reads, both with that timeout,
    and
    print which entries it added and
    which it found already there. Refuse with a message that says no child host
    is
    registered when the driver registry lists none, refuse with a message that
    names every supported child host when the child host is missing and several
    are
    registered,
    or is not a supported child host, refuse with a message that names the
    child host when its
    child driver offers no
    starter tools, and print the load error and exit non-zero when the
    agent file
    exists and does not load for a reason other than a missing starter entry,
    and
    print the error that names both child hosts and exit
    non-zero when the agent file already holds a medium tier on another
    child host
    than
    the given child host. On subzero tasks, read the task record of each task
    and print
    the
    id,
    agent, task status and creation time of every task. On subzero attach, read
    the launch spec of the task, refuse when the task has no recorded
    launch spec or its task status is running, and otherwise ask the
    driver registry for
    the attach command of the child driver of the child host of the
    agent definition of
    the task, start it, and refuse with a message that names the child host
    when
    that
    child driver offers none. On subzero show, export the child session of the
    task
    through the session export of the child driver of the child host of the
    task,
    refusing with a message that names the child host when that child driver
    offers
    none,
    and say that an abandoned task has no result. Each
    command ends by printing its output and exiting.
  }

  constraints {
    The Cli passes its working directory to the delegation service as its
    fallback
    project root, and receives from the delegation service the project root
    that it
    resolved, which comes from AgentConfig in the order its constraints give,
    for
    its own use by init.

    A delegation from the Cli must carry no parent session id, because a
    command
    line has no conversation, and no reply budget, because the Cli prints the
    result whole to a terminal that has no inline limit.

    The attach command must be refused while the task status of the task is
    running, because the start-up sweep has already marked the task of a dead
    owner abandoned. It must also be refused with a message that no launch spec
    was recorded when the task record has none.

    Cli depends on DelegationService for the delegation, the status line and
    the result text that it prints, on TaskStore for the
    task record, on TaskCore for the launch spec, the attach command and the
    session export, on AgentConfig for the agent file, the starter entries and
    the
    errors it shows, and on the driver registry of Kernel for the child driver
    of a
    child host. Cli must not depend on any particular child driver or
    parent adapter, and
    it names no child host. The entry point of the command line process is
    outside
    Cli:
    it imports the child drivers that process needs and registers them with
    Kernel,
    and Cli imports none of them.
  }

  cases {
    Attach on a task whose task status is running is refused. On a settled task
    it
    asks the driver registry for the attach command of the child driver of its
    child host
    and builds it from the launch spec, and on a task with no recorded
    launch spec
    it is refused. When the child driver of its child host offers no
    attach command, it
    is refused with a message that names the child host.

    Subzero run against a scripted pi writes the task record with task.json,
    events.jsonl and turns/1.json, appends an index line and prints the result.

    Subzero run with an unknown agent name runs the fallback agent, which the
    load requires. Subzero run with
    no agent name runs the general agent. Subzero init with the child host pi,
    in
    an
    agent file whose medium tier is on the child host claude, prints the error
    that
    names both child hosts, exits non-zero and writes nothing.

    Subzero init with the child host pi, when the prerequisites check of its
    child driver returns a message that says pi was not found, prints that
    message,
    exits non-zero and writes no agent file. When that child driver offers no
    prerequisites check, init goes on.

    Subzero init in a project with no agent file creates the agent file with a
    medium tier on the one registered child host, the given model and the
    thinking level
    medium, and a general agent and a read-only fallback agent, each with a
    timeout
    of 1200 seconds. Run again, it adds nothing, changes no line and says that
    all
    three entries are already there. With a general agent already in the file,
    it
    adds only the fallback agent and leaves the general agent as it was.
  }

  interface {
    Offer five commands: subzero init with a model and the named options
    host, which names the child host,
    timeout and thinking, subzero run with a brief and the named option agent,
    which may be left out,
    subzero tasks, subzero attach with a task id,
    and subzero show with a task id.

    Make the child session of a task, its transcript and its task record
    reachable
    by task id after the parent session has ended.
  }
}
